# Secure dependency selection

Install packages in the app that needs them (`admin/`, `client/`, or `api/`). Root `package.json` only forwards scripts; do not `npm install` there.

```bash
# ❌ BAD — install at the repo root, or add a second UI kit in admin
npm install some-ui-lib

# ✅ GOOD — from the package that uses it
cd admin && npm install <pkg>
cd client && npm install -D eslint prettier
cd api && npm install <pkg>
npm audit
```

- Prefer the current stable release, not alpha/beta/nightly, unless the user asks.
- Prefer maintained packages. Skip ones with known high or critical vulnerabilities; pick a patched version or a safer alternative.
- Do not add a library the app already covers (admin UI follows `shadcn-only-ui`).
- Lockfiles: `admin/package-lock.json`, `client/package-lock.json`, `api/package-lock.json`.
- After install, run that package’s `typecheck` / `lint` (when present), and say so if `npm audit` reports a new blocker.
